  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Sikorsky Aircraft obligated $2.9B in federal contract dollars in FY2026 to date. Sikorsky Aircraft received 12,683 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $232K, and obligations are down 39.1% year over year. Current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date). The Department of Defense is by far the largest buyer, obligating $2.9B, followed by the Department of Homeland Security with $76.7M and the Department of Justice with $8.3M. Aircraft Manufacturing is the dominant market for Sikorsky Aircraft, receiving $2.5B in obligations, supported by Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $331M. Smaller markets in FY2026 to date include Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $25.8M and Aircraft Engine and Engine Parts Manufacturing at $21.8M. This snapshot shows concentration in aviation-related work and a current-year obligation level below prior fiscal-year peaks, with FY23 at $5.3B and FY21 at $4.9B.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are Sikorsky Aircraft obligations by agency?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the primary buyer, obligating $2.9B in FY2026 to date. The Department of Homeland Security and the Department of Justice follow at $76.7M and $8.3M respectively. This distribution shows heavy reliance on one federal customer for the majority of contract dollars."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are Sikorsky Aircraft's main product and service markets?",
        "body": "Aircraft Manufacturing is the largest market for Sikorsky Aircraft at $2.5B in FY2026 to date. Other significant markets include Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $331M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $25.8M. Remaining NAICS categories each account for materially smaller obligation totals."
      }
    ]
